Weathered Sentinels attacks only players who attacked you (Commander Duels v0.9.0), in every
format.

Reason: at the pin, the card's limit was a replacement of DECLARE_ATTACKER that applied to every
creature its controller declared, not only the Sentinels, and read its watcher's two arguments the
wrong way round, asking whether the controller had attacked that player. The controller's own
record is cleared as their turn begins, so in a first combat it limited nothing: once any opponent
had attacked you, the Sentinels could attack every player, planeswalker and battle; in an extra
combat the controller's creatures could not attack a player already attacked that turn. The hint
named the players the controller had attacked. The limit is now a restriction on the Sentinels alone: while it has defender and only
its own ability lets it attack, it may attack only a player who attacked its controller during
that player's last turn (no planeswalkers or battles); without defender, or with another effect
letting it attack as though it didn't have defender, it attacks as any creature. The hint names
the players who attacked you. Applies after 0009, which changed the watcher's bookkeeping for
team games and is unchanged here. The human player's defender choice offers only the defenders
the attacker can attack (PlayerImpl.declareAttacker refused the others without a word), so a
seat choosing where the Sentinels attack sees only the players who attacked it; with one, no
choice is asked.
Upstream: none.
Remove when: XMage limits the Sentinels alone, reading its watcher the right way round.

